        "original_id": "8cf53a2b-a08e-5783-83cc-ed309ae0b8e8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Arthur Saint-Léon\n- Organizations: Mariinsky Ballet, St. Petersburg Imperial Ballet, Mariinsky Theatre, Vaganova Ballet Academy\n- Places: Paris, Saint Petersburg, Russia\n- Roles: Maître de Ballet\n- Works: Coppélia\n\nFacts:\n- Arthur Saint-Léon was born on 17 September 1821 in Paris and died on 2 September 1870.\n- The Mariinsky Ballet was founded in the 18th century and was originally known as the Imperial Russian Ballet.\n- Arthur Saint-Léon served as Maître de Ballet of the St. Petersburg Imperial Ballet from 1859 until 1869.\n- Arthur Saint-Léon is famous for creating the choreography of the ballet Coppélia.\n- The Mariinsky Ballet is the resident classical ballet company of the Mariinsky Theatre in Saint Petersburg, Russia.\n- The Mariinsky Ballet is one of the world's leading ballet companies.\n- The Mariinsky Ballet is the parent company of the Vaganova Ballet Academy, a leading international ballet school.",
